<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish EBS ups saving rates, defers mortgage raise.</title>
<headline>Irish EBS ups saving rates, defers mortgage raise.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's EBS Building Society said on Tuesday it was increasing savings rates by a minimum of 0.25 percentage points from October 1, and was raising its mortgage rate by 0.25 percentage points from January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Several Irish financial insitutions including AIB, Bank of Ireland and Irish Permanent raised their lending rates recently in response to a tightening in Irish money market rates.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
